<title>ITALY: Italy to sell 3rd ENI tranche by autumn.</title>
<headline>Italy to sell 3rd ENI tranche by autumn.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian Treasury Minister Carlo Azeglio Ciampi said the sale of a third tranche in state-controlled energy group ENI will take place by this autumn.</p>
<p>&quot;I confirm that sometime in autumn this year there will be the placing of a third ENI tranche,&quot; Ciampi said, addressing the public works commission of the upper house Senate.</p>
<p>The Treasury sold a second tranche of shares in ENI in November 1996 bringing its stake in the group down to 69 percent. An initial 15 percent stake was placed on the market in November 1995.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +392 66129589</p>
